From 1f535520a3d0a7ceb3b82e10b0037d85176f7320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "crychic.tan" <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:52:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qosify: clear bridger blacklist synchronously on shutdown

qosify blacklists the devices it manages in bridger, so their traffic is
not offloaded past its shaping and DSCP marking. On shutdown it sends an
empty blacklist with an asynchronous ubus call and closes the connection
right after it. ubusd does not read the rest of a socket once it sees
the connection closed, so the request is often lost and the devices stay
without hardware offload until bridger restarts. Turning QoS off through
uCentral ("/etc/init.d/qosify stop") left eth1 blacklisted in 6 of 20
cases on an MT7981 AP with WED.

Add a qosify package patch that sends this request synchronously, with a
1 s timeout.

Signed-off-by: crychic.tan <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
---
 ...-blacklist-synchronously-on-shutdown.patch | 39 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/network/config/qosify/patches/100-ubus-clear-bridger-blacklist-synchronously-on-shutdown.patch

diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/patches/100-ubus-clear-bridger-blacklist-synchronously-on-shutdown.patch b/package/network/config/qosify/patches/100-ubus-clear-bridger-blacklist-synchronously-on-shutdown.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..a0da43e69a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/patches/100-ubus-clear-bridger-blacklist-synchronously-on-shutdown.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+From: crychic.tan <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
+Subject: [PATCH] ubus: clear the bridger blacklist synchronously on shutdown
+
+qosify_ubus_stop() sends the empty bridger blacklist with
+ubus_invoke_async() and closes the ubus connection right after it.
+ubusd does not read what is left in the socket of a client once it sees
+the connection closed: uloop marks the fd as eof on EPOLLRDHUP before
+the read callback runs, and client_cb() skips reading when eof is set.
+So the request is lost whenever ubusd has not read it before qosify
+closes the connection, and the devices of qosify stay blacklisted in
+bridger, without hardware offload, until bridger is restarted.
+
+On an MT7981 AP with WED, "/etc/init.d/qosify stop", which is how
+uCentral turns QoS off, left eth1 blacklisted in 6 of 20 cases.
+
+Send the request synchronously on shutdown. ubus_invoke() polls the
+socket itself, so it works after uloop_run() has returned, and the 1 s
+timeout bounds the wait if bridger does not answer.
+
+Signed-off-by: crychic.tan <crychic.tan@cybertan.com.tw>
+---
+ ubus.c |    6 +++++-
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+--- a/ubus.c
++++ b/ubus.c
+@@ -400,7 +400,11 @@ void qosify_ubus_update_bridger(bool shu
+ 		qosify_iface_get_devices(&b);
+ 	blobmsg_close_array(&b, c);
+ 
+-	ubus_invoke_async(&conn.ctx, id, "set_blacklist", b.head, &req);
++	/* ubusd drops requests it has not read when the connection is closed */
++	if (shutdown)
++		ubus_invoke(&conn.ctx, id, "set_blacklist", b.head, NULL, NULL, 1000);
++	else
++		ubus_invoke_async(&conn.ctx, id, "set_blacklist", b.head, &req);
+ }
+ 
+ int qosify_ubus_init(void)
-- 
